"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[69583],{569583:e=>{e.exports='# Find a System Case\n\nHow to find or retrieve a **system case** by ID (either uuid or short-ID like sys-1234), by name/description, or by listing system cases with **filters** and **sorting**. Use when the user asks to view, get, or open a specific system case, or to list system cases (e.g. open system cases, high severity, system cases for a datasource/rule, newest first).\n\n## Common questions and filter/sort conditions\n\nUse **apiListLakewatchSystemCases** (it lists SYSTEM_CASE / system cases only). Pass `null` or empty for any filter you don\'t need.\n\n| User question / intent                            | Filters / sort to use                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| “Show me open system cases”                       | `state: ["OPEN"]`, others empty array or null                                                           |\n| “List resolved/dismissed system cases”            | `state: ["RESOLVED"]`, others empty array or null                                                       |\n| “High severity system cases”                      | `severity: ["HIGH"]`, others empty array or null                                                        |\n| “System cases that need attention” / “unassigned” | `unassigned: true`, `state: ["OPEN"]` or `[]`, others empty array or null                               |\n| “System cases assigned to me”                     | `assigneeId: "<user id>"`, others null                                                                  |\n| “System cases for datasource X”                   | `resourceType: "Datasource"`, `resourceId: "<datasource id>"` (or use resourceType only), others null   |\n| “System cases for rule X”                         | `resourceType: "Rule"`, `resourceId: "<rule id>"`, others null                                          |\n| “System cases with ‘pipeline’ in the title”       | `titleSearch: "pipeline"`, others null                                                                  |\n| “System cases created before last week”           | `createdBefore: "<ISO timestamp>"`, others null                                                         |\n| “Newest system cases first”                       | `orderByColumn: "created_at"`, `orderByDirection: "desc"`, filters as needed                            |\n| “Recently updated system cases”                   | `orderByColumn: "last_modified_at"`, `orderByDirection: "desc"`, filters as needed                      |\n| “Open high-severity system cases”                 | `state: ["OPEN"]`, `severity: ["HIGH"]`, others empty array or null                                     |\n| “All system cases” (no filter)                    | `state: []`, `severity: []`, other filters null; use `orderByColumn`/`orderByDirection` if sort desired |\n\n**Filter values**: `state` and `severity` accept **multiple values** (arrays). `state` — OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, MITIGATED, RESOLVED, DUPLICATE, STATE_UNSPECIFIED. `severity` — INFORMATIONAL, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL, CASE_SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED. `resourceType` — e.g. Datasource, Rule (or null for all). Pass empty array for state/severity to omit.\n\n## User provides a system case ID\n\nWhen the user gives a system case uuid ID or a short ID like sys-1234 directly, call `apiGetLakewatchResourceById` with `resourceType: "system-case"` and `resourceId` set to that ID.\n\n```json\n{\n  "thoughts": "User provided system case ID. Retrieving the system case directly.",\n  "resourceType": "system-case",\n  "resourceId": "alert-id-here"\n}\n```\n\n## User provides a system case name or description\n\nWhen the user references a system case by description or type:\n\n1. Call **apiListLakewatchSystemCases** with `thoughts`, `limit` (e.g. 100), and the filter/sort that matches the user\'s intent (see table above).\n2. Search the list for a system case matching the description; match case-insensitively and allow partial matches.\n3. Extract the system case ID from the response.\n4. Call **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** with `resourceType: "system-case"` and that `resourceId`.\n\nIf the user\'s request is to search more generally (full search across description and comments) you can use the apiSearchLakewatchCases tool. This will return results with a bit of context around each match. You can then use apiGetLakewatchResourceById to get the whole case for each match that seems relevant.\n\n**Filtering**: `titleSearch`, `state` (array of values; empty to omit), `severity` (array of values; empty to omit), `unassigned`, `createdBefore` (ISO timestamp), `assigneeId`, `resourceType`, `resourceId`. State values: OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, MITIGATED, RESOLVED, DUPLICATE, STATE_UNSPECIFIED. Severity: INFORMATIONAL, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL, CASE_SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED. Pass null for other unused filters.\n\n**Sorting**: `orderByColumn` (`created_at` | `last_modified_at`), `orderByDirection` (`asc` | `desc`).\n\n**Multiple matches**: Present all with ID (prefer the sys-xxx short ID when displaying to the user) and distinguishing info; ask the user which one they want.\n\n**No match**: Tell the user no system case matched; suggest listing all system cases or trying a different description.\n'}}]);
